<urn:atm:triage:finding/BA5-QA1-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BA5-QA1-003" ;
  triage:title "rusqlite boundary leak: atm-http-runtime adds a raw rusqlite dev-dependency and Connection, 8 lint-boundaries errors" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-1 (quality-mgr, ruthless-boundary-qa RBQA-BA5-F001 critical, arch-qa ARCH-001 blocking, rust-qa-agent QA-003, req-qa ATM-QA-003 citing REQ-CORE-STORE-003), PR #1407 @ b617a9eab, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1407#issuecomment-5642789392. This sprint's own diff adds rusqlite = { version = \"0.33.0\", features = [\"bundled\"] } as a dev-dependency to crates/atm-http-runtime/Cargo.toml:47 (absent on the BA.3 base and in BA.4's own diff), and new BA.5 test helpers in herdr_queue_wake.rs (~lines 1409, 1415, 1430, 1437, 4504) open a raw rusqlite::Connection and hand-write SQL against mail_message_states columns. just lint-boundaries fails with 8 errors: only atm-storage-rusqlite may depend on/import rusqlite; boundaries/atm-http-runtime/http-runtime.toml was not updated and rusqlite was not added to the manifest-dependency-allowlist. fenix's ruling (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1407#issuecomment-5642806916): STANDS -- remove both; read/seed rows through the PendingNudgeStore/MessageStore trait surface or atm-runtime-test-support. The boundary TOML and allowlist are not relaxed." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "boundary" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-http-runtime/Cargo.toml, crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
